; A PLAIN loose-list mint (`[* bar]` over a non-exposable element) synthesizes the wasm wrapper
; class `BarList`; a user rule of a DIFFERENT shape (`bar_list = tstr`) snake_case-claims that same
; ident. Under --wasm=true both would be defined in `wasm/src/generated/mod.rs` — the user `pub type
; BarList = String;` alias and the synthesized `pub struct BarList(...)` wrapper. The DIRECT-claim
; leg of `non_empty_wrapper_name_collisions` owns this class: it scans every PLAIN use that mints a
; loose `<Elem>List` (a `*`-occurrence array, a map or table keys() wrapper, a rest row's keys(), a
; rest tail) and rejects an incompatible claim in the list family's own voice, naming the use that
; mints the class and the two remedies. It fires in `finalize`, ahead of the generation-time
; duplicate-ident backstop that formerly reported this by ident alone. A rule that IS `[* bar]` of
; the same element is that builder, not a collision.
bar = [x: uint]
bar_list = tstr
holder = { xs: [* bar] }
